---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Configuration"
  description="opsrun.yaml inventory, concurrency, timeouts, audit, approval defaults, and secrets."
  path="/docs/configuration"
>
  <p>
    Pass a config file with <code>--config</code> or set <code>OPSRUN_CONFIG</code>.
    Values are overridden by <code>OPSRUN_*</code> environment variables and then by
    CLI flags.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sample">Sample opsrun.yaml</h2>
  <pre><code>hosts:
  - name: web-1
    address: 10.0.1.10
    port: 22
    user: ops
    identity_file: ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
    groups: [web]

  - name: db-1
    address: 10.0.2.10
    port: 22
    user: ops
    identity_file: ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
    proxy_jump: bastion.internal:22
    groups: [db]

concurrency:
  global_max_connections: 50
  per_host_max_sessions: 2
  max_parallel_steps: 10

timeouts:
  connect: 10s
  command: 5m
  idle: 1m

audit:
  log_path: ./audit/opsrun-audit.jsonl
  signing_key_path: ""

approval:
  mode: per_step
  timeout: 5m

secrets:
  env_prefix: OPSRUN_SECRET_
  files_dir: ""</code></pre>

  <h2 id="hosts">Hosts and groups</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>name</code> — inventory id referenced by plans and audit</li>
    <li><code>address</code>, <code>port</code>, <code>user</code></li>
    <li><code>identity_file</code> — private key path</li>
    <li><code>proxy_jump</code> — optional bastion</li>
    <li><code>groups</code> — labels used by runbook <code>targets: - group:</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="concurrency">Concurrency</h2>
  <p>
    Cap global SSH connections, per-host sessions, and parallel DAG steps. Keep these
    conservative on shared bastions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="timeouts">Timeouts</h2>
  <p>
    Connect, command, and idle timeouts are Go duration strings (<code>10s</code>,
    <code>5m</code>). Step-level <code>timeout=</code> on <code>opsrun:run</code> can
    tighten a single action.
  </p>

  <h2 id="audit">Audit</h2>
  <p>
    <code>log_path</code> is the JSONL audit sink. Optional
    <code>signing_key_path</code> enables Ed25519 signing of records.
  </p>

  <h2 id="approval">Approval defaults</h2>
  <p>
    Runbook front matter can override mode and timeout. Per-step directives can override
    again. Modes: <code>none</code>, <code>per_step</code>, <code>all</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="secrets">Secrets</h2>
  <p>
    Environment variables under <code>secrets.env_prefix</code> (default
    <code>OPSRUN_SECRET_</code>) and optional files under <code>files_dir</code> feed the
    secret provider. Mark runbook vars with <code>secret: true</code> so interpolated
    values never appear in logs or audit plaintext.
  </p>

  <h2 id="host-keys">SSH host keys</h2>
  <p>
    Host-key verification against <code>known_hosts</code> is required. Disabling it is
    an explicit, warned opt-out. Prefer fixing known_hosts over bypassing checks.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
